 {
  "tag_name": "v0.0.1",
  "name": "OpenDJDecks 0.0.1",
  "draft": false,
  "prerelease": true,
  "html_url": "https://github.com/nurkert/OpenDJDecks/releases/tag/v0.0.1",
  "published_at": "2026-11-06T16:54:58Z",
  "body": "First public preview of OpenDJDecks — open-source DJ software for macOS, Linux and the Raspberry Pi.\n\n## Downloads\n\n| Platform | File |\n|---|---|\n| macOS (Apple Silicon) | `OpenDJDecks-*-macos-arm64.dmg` |\n| macOS (Intel) | `OpenDJDecks-*-macos-x86_64.dmg` |\n| Debian 12+, Ubuntu 22.04+ (x86_64) | `opendjdecks_*_amd64.deb` |\n| Debian 12+, Ubuntu 22.04+, Raspberry Pi OS 64-bit (arm64) | `opendjdecks_*_arm64.deb` |\n| Any Linux | `OpenDJDecks-*.AppImage`, `opendjdecks-*-linux-*.tar.gz` |\n| Raspberry Pi standalone (kiosk) | `opendjdecks-pi-*.tar.gz` — see `packaging/raspberry-pi/README.md` |\n\nmacOS: the app is not notarised yet. On first start, right-click the app → **Open**, or run\n`xattr -dr com.apple.quarantine \"/Applications/OpenDJDecks.app\"`.\n\n## What's in it\n\n- Library with analysis (BPM/beatgrid, key, waveforms, phrases), playlists, smart playlists and sets with flow and transition hints\n- USB sticks that stay in sync automatically, in the OpenDJDecks format\n- Perform with 2 or 4 decks, sync, keylock, FX, sampler; mappings for compatible DJ controllers\n- One-button recording with automatic tracklist\n- English and German\n\n## Known limitations\n\nSee [docs/verification.md](https://github.com/nurkert/OpenDJDecks/blob/main/docs/verification.md): the controller mappings and the Raspberry Pi kiosk still need testing on hardware.\n",
  "id": 436759835,
